{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8948-2",
  "summary": "php5, php7.0, php7.2, php7.4 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "USN-8948-1 fixed vulnerabilities in Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS,\nUbuntu 26.04 LTS and Ubuntu 26.10. This provides the corrosponding updates\nin Ubuntu 14.04 LTS, Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS and Ubuntu 20.04\nLTS.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly handled out-of-memory conditions\nwhile processing requests. A remote attacker could use this issue to\nexecute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-109618)\n\nIt was discovered that PHP incorrectly managed internal request state\nacross worker reuse. A remote attacker could use this issue to execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-109619)",
  "aliases": [],
